Unless you threw a cbgvba bs pbashfvba, it's probably nothing you did.

As you note, liches don't eat, so they won't be confused by hunger.

However, if you're on a level with a poly trap, there cuold be a number
of creatures roaming about that could have confused your pet. I just lost
a perfectly good Valk yesterday because my cat had eaten a doppelganger
corpse and become an arch-lich, then an hour later a black light exploded
in his face.

If you can, just get a level away (preferably up :) from your lich for a
few hundred turns. If he goes feral, that's still easier to deal with than
having to put down a pet.

